  "findings": [
    "All three original GDS files pass full geometry in the enabled ORFS deck, full Volare KLayout deck and full Magic deck.",
    "Both full geometry engines detect injected poly-width and Metal1-width faults.",
    "Magic misses the isolated poly antenna fault; the supplemental KLayout poly check rejects it and the just-over-limit boundary. All three reference poly checks pass.",
    "Magic native antenna accepts counter/UART and reports three APB contact-stage findings with 24 feedback shapes.",
    "The independent via3 diagnostic reports no violations. A separate measurement-only run finds six gate-connected via3 cuts, each 0.04 square micrometres; the three relevant gate networks each have 0.213 square micrometres of gate area and ratio 0.187793427230047. This disagreement remains unresolved.",
    "Density was remeasured using the original declared die rectangle. The v1 cell-bounding-box measurements are superseded and never accepted.",
    "601 published periphery rows and all 165 captured rule documents are pinned. Deck text hits are search candidates only; applicability and executed coverage remain unreviewed."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Reconcile every required manual/deck rule, including exclusions and non-DRC obligations.",
    "Qualify every antenna etch stage and resolve the APB native/independent discrepancy with fault controls.",
    "Resolve applicable density interpretation and fill requirements with complete native/supplemental execution.",
    "Run strict final-GDS device, body, supply and port LVS with deliberate connectivity faults.",
    "Integrate the complete coverage gate into the application and verify Windows/Linux delivery."
  ],
  "rejected_experiments": [
    "Antenna/density v1 used the current cell extent for density instead of the declared die.",
    "Poly antenna v1 omitted visible completion output; those captures were not accepted.",
    "Geometry-fault v1 assumed a 1 nm database unit and stopped before native execution."
  ],
